    "q-124222": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124222",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 6 \\\\ -4 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-5)-6\\cdot (-4)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-5+5+8=8.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
